#X text 50 88 [incdec] is an increment/decrement button GUI. Click the upper half to add the step size to the current value and the lower half to subtract it. Hold shift while clicking for 1/10 of the step size. Values are clipped to the object's range., f 66;
#X text 43 152 click and hold =>, f 10;
#X obj 160 148 else/incdec 20 30 1 -1e+06 1e+06 0 0 255 255 255 0 0 0 empty empty 1 0 0;
#X floatatom 160 205 7 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X text 215 205 current value;
#X text 300 148 It can also lay its arrows out left/right \, repeat while you hold it down \, and send 1/-1 instead of a running count - see [pd modes]., f 32;
#N canvas 202 161 1400 688 step-range 0;
#X text 30 20 The step size sets how much a click adds or subtracts and the range clips the result. Shift-clicking uses 1/10 of the step size \, so a step of 1 gives you 0.1 increments., f 56;
#X text 30 90 set the step size:;
#X msg 149 91 step 0.5;
#X msg 219 91 step 5;
#X msg 279 91 step 0.01;
#X text 52 135 set the range:;
#X msg 149 138 range -10 10;
#X msg 244 138 range 0 127;
#X msg 334 138 range -1 1;
